  "description": "Brothas Doobie is the second studio album by Los Angeles–based hip hop group Funkdoobiest. It was released on July 4, 1995, via Epic Records. This was the final album featuring back-up MC and hypeman Tomahawk Funk, who left the group after this release. The album contains the controversial track \"Superhoes\", which also appeared in the soundtrack to the film Friday, starring N.W.A's Ice Cube.",
